__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"CHANGELOG",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}}),e.unseenEntries=function(o,s=t){return null===o?s.slice(0,1):s.filter(t=>t.id>o)},Object.defineProperty(e,"latestChangelogId",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const t=[{id:31,date:'2026-11-07',notes:['Fitbit works again: connect it in Settings to sync steps, calories and sleep.','New Recovery card on the Day tab for Fitbit users: a morning readiness score plus resting heart rate, HRV, blood oxygen, breathing rate and skin temperature, each compared with your own last 30 nights. It needs about a week of nights to learn your normal.','Reports show the same readings, and weekly and monthly reports chart resting heart rate and HRV.']},{id:30,date:'2026-11-05',notes:['Planks, holds, walks and other cardio added to a workout are now timed instead of counted in reps. A short hold is logged in seconds; anything 2 minutes or longer, like an incline walk, is logged in minutes.','Any exercise can be switched between reps and time with "Exercise type" (Timed or Weighted timed), during a workout or in the program editor.']},{id:29,date:'2026-11-04',notes:['Reordering exercises: the exercise you drag now follows your finger, and stays within the list.','In the program editor, the page no longer scrolls while you drag an exercise, so the drag isn\'t cancelled halfway.']},{id:28,date:'2026-11-04',notes:['New migraine log. Turn it on in Settings \u2192 What you track (or by adding Migraine as a condition), then log attacks from the Check-in: when it started and ended, how bad it got, what it felt like, any aura, what you took and whether it worked.','Each attack is checked against the international migraine criteria (ICHD-3), and reports count headache days, medication days and suspected triggers, and flag the levels where doctors suggest preventive treatment or watch for painkiller overuse. Sources are listed in the report.']},{id:27,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['The sleep goal is now 8 hours a night for everyone. Reports, the day\'s grade and the leaderboard count a night under 8 hours as short. You can still change yours in Settings \u2192 Body and devices.']},{id:26,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['Water now counts on the Leaderboard: 10% of the score, from each day\'s water against your daily target, plus its own Water category. Nutrition and logging are now 20% and 10%.','Reports show your water too: the day\'s total, or for a week or month the daily average and how many days you hit your target.']},{id:25,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['Water has its own switch in Settings \u2192 What you track, so you can track water without the food diary. With food off, water gets its own view on the Day tab.']},{id:24,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['The Leaderboard\'s exercise score now counts lifting days towards your weekly goal. Cardio no longer counts as a lifting day; it still counts towards the 150 cardio minutes a week.']},{id:23,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['The Leaderboard now has medals. Use the arrows under Week or Month to go back through past weeks and months: once one is over, its top three get gold, silver and bronze.','A new Medals card counts everyone\'s medals and lists who won each week and month. Tap one to open its board.']},{id:22,date:'2026-11-03',notes:['Settings \u2192 Body and devices has a Sleep goal. Pick 7 to 9 hours a night, and your reports and the leaderboard measure sleep against it.','Foods whose label serving is a count, like "5 nuggets", can now be logged one piece at a time.']},{id:21,date:'2026-11-02',notes:['Settings \u2192 Recipes app makes a link code for the new Recipes app. Paste it there to see nutrition per serving and log what you cooked straight into your Food diary.']},{id:20,date:'2026-10-30',notes:["The Leaderboard's Score by day chart now stops at yesterday. Today's score is still filling in, so it showed up as a drop at the end of every line."]},{id:19,date:'2026-10-27',notes:['The Leaderboard widget showed nothing in the last build. It is fixed and now comes as two widgets, "Leaderboard today" and "Leaderboard this week": add the one you want (or both) from the widget gallery.']},{id:18,date:'2026-10-27',notes:['The Habits widget is more compact and groups habits by morning, afternoon and evening. It also comes in a small size that shows the part of the day you are in.','The Leaderboard widget can show today or this week: long-press it, tap Edit Widget and pick the period.']},{id:17,date:'2026-10-27',notes:['The Today widget now shows fiber and your next habits too, and comes in a large size where you can tick those habits off.',"The Leaderboard widget shows everyone's score for today, and comes in a medium size."]},{id:16,date:'2026-10-27',notes:['A habit can fill itself in from a linked practice app: edit the habit, turn on "Fill in from \u2026" and pick the minutes a day. It ticks once you have practiced that long, and shows the minutes so far.','A public habit filled in that way also shows its practice minutes on the leaderboard.']},{id:15,date:'2026-10-27',notes:['Home screen widgets: Today (calories, protein, steps, water), Habits, Water, Next workout and Leaderboard. Long-press the home screen, tap +, and search for Health.','Tick off a habit or add a drink straight from its widget, without opening the app.','Lock screen widgets: protein, steps and water rings, habits left, and calories with your deficit.','The first time, a widget shows a short code: enter it in Settings \u2192 Widgets to pair it with your account.']},{id:14,date:'2026-10-26',notes:['Workouts: a lift no longer drops 10% for "no progress" when the slow sessions were split by more than two weeks off. A rough first day back is not counted as a stall.']},{id:13,date:'2026-10-26',notes:['Weekly, monthly and overall reports now chart the period day by day: steps, energy balance, weight, sleep, calories, protein and training. Overall reports chart it week by week.','The exported PDF has the same charts, headline numbers up top, topic headings like the report screen, a bar beside each nutrient and habit, and page numbers.']},{id:12,date:'2026-10-25',notes:["A blood pressure reading's time taken now fills in when you start typing the numbers, so it no longer shows when the screen was opened. A time you change yourself is kept."]},{id:11,date:'2026-10-25',notes:['The report page is tidier: cards are grouped under Body, Sleep, Nutrition, Food, Training and Habits & wellbeing, and each nutrient takes less room, with where it came from and why it matters a tap away.']},{id:10,date:'2026-10-25',notes:['Faster still: the diary and Activity each load in one request instead of several, and the server sends less data to your phone.']},{id:9,date:'2026-10-25',notes:['Training: opening a recent workout now lays it out exercise by exercise, with each set on its own numbered row showing the weight, reps and RIR.']},{id:8,date:'2026-10-25',notes:['The app opens faster: your diary, check-in, activity and leaderboard show what you last saw straight away and update a moment later.']},{id:7,date:'2026-10-25',notes:['Leaderboard: opening Activity, Habits or Nutrition now indents what is inside, with a line down the side, so it is clear which rows belong to it.']},{id:6,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['Exercise demos are more accurate: the cable lateral raise, serratus wall slide and kneeling cable pulldown have their own pictures, and warm-up sets show the exercise they warm up for.','Renaming an exercise in a program no longer loses its last weights.']},{id:5,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['Workouts are easier to read mid-set: bigger set numbers, targets, last-time figures and rest timer.','Less small print on each exercise. The reason behind a target is a tap away (\u201cwhy \u203a\u201d), the date of last time sits above the Last column, and warm-up notes moved to More options.']},{id:4,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['Log \u2192 Activity: last night\'s sleep now shows time asleep and in bed, efficiency, bedtime and wake, and a bar of deep, core, REM and awake time. Stages fill in from tonight\'s sync on.','Leaderboard: the sleep goal is now 8 hours.']},{id:3,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['Leaderboard: open Sleep under Activity for the full breakdown: time asleep and in bed, deep sleep, typical bedtime and wake, and nights that reached your goal.']},{id:2,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['Workouts: a set that beats your heaviest set or estimated max gets a PR badge, and the exercise card lists the records broken so far.','Workouts: the program card and preview estimate how long a session takes from your own pace, and during a workout the header shows when it should end.','Tapping the "Rest over" notification opens the workout on the next set, ready to type.','Leaderboard: steps, getting up, exercise and sleep now sit together under an Activity drop-down, and sleep counts toward the score.','Leaderboard: "Getting up" counts the hours you were up and moving (Apple Watch stand hours, goal 12) under Activity. The app asks for permission to read them on its next sync.','Leaderboard: the Day tab has arrows to step back through past days.']},{id:1,date:'2026-10-23',notes:['A "What\'s new" note like this one now appears after each update.']}];const o=()=>Math.max(0,...t.map(t=>t.id))},730,[]);
